<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Ganadero cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Ganadero cut.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- ING Barings analysts Nuno Fernandes, Petru Vaduva and Eugenia Vargas have reduced their ratings on both preferred and common American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) for Colombia's Banco Ganadero to hold from buy.</p>
<p>-- They wrote in an April 8 report that the downgrade was based on the common and preferred ADRs' &quot;solid investment performance in the past 12 months.</p>
<p>-- &quot;We see limited returns of 12 and 16 percent until December 1997, respectively.&quot;</p>
<p>-- The common shares' ADR was up 1/8 to 33-1/8 and the preferred shares' ADR rose 3/8 to 26-1/8.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
